  "body": "What happens: the post-merge batch gate is red on main `983f527bd`.\nRun: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/44258092076\nFailed step: \"Batch gate tier\", 2 failed of 859 steps, wall 48.8 min.\n\nFailures:\n\n1. Step 553, `app suites: microarc_test_part`, test `a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a` (FAIL in 4 s). This suite checks posted output. For that reason the priority is `P1`.\n2. `ui suites: lib`, test `egui_app::tests::guide_projects::demo_projects_build_and_load_with_valid_paths` (FAIL in 76 s).\n\nContext:\n\n- The earlier run on main `1d3d93541` (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/44253769789) had failure 2 only: 1 failed of 856 steps. Failure 2 was thus on main before the last merge batch.\n- Failure 1 is new with the batch `e87658f44..983f527bd` (#2068, #2386 Tormach wrapped A, #2035 adaptive stock ring). #2386 changed the Tormach wrapped A post and is the first PR to examine.\n- The `camcraft-ui` lib tests were green in local quick gates on Windows today with main `983f527bd` merged in (PR #2185, PR #2414). Failure 2 can be specific to the runner. This is not confirmed.\n- The log of the run shows the step result only. It does not show the assert text of the two tests.\n\nNote: the report job of the workflow was skipped. It did not open this issue. An agent opened it by hand.\n\nRelated: #2473 (Tormach post, a move without an A angle in an indexed operation).\n\nDone when: the two tests are green on main, and the next post-merge run is green.\n",
